// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The university crest, embedded in the document rather than linked from it.
//
// The letterhead loaded it from https://iguc.net/images/site-icon.png. That
// works in a browser with a connection, and fails everywhere that matters: an
// email client blocking remote images, which most do by default; an attachment
// opened on a plane; an applicant at an embassy with no data. In each of those
// the university's own crest rendered as a broken-image icon at the top of its
// formal offer of admission.
//
// So it travels with the document. 156 pixels — twice the 78pt it is drawn at,
// so a printer has something to work with — costing about 68KB on a letter
// nobody sends in bulk. A self-contained document is worth more than the bytes.
//
// Regenerate after replacing public/images/site-icon.png; that file is the only
// copy that should ever be edited.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

export const CREST_DATA_URI =
  'data:image/png;base64,';
